50,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"The candidates are A: Central Study Commons, B: Media Production Center, C: Campus Path Network, and D: Laboratory Ventilation Upgrade. I favor A.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Victoria,,A aligns with the booking data. It provides the general-purpose space we lack and avoids the specialist room waste.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"C is too weather-dependent. D is a mechanical project, which Kenji noted is becoming expensive and prone to delays.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"B requires AV equipment, and I found we have no renewal reserve for that. A seems the most fiscally stable.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"D would help the technicians' manual routines, but A is a conversion of an existing hall, which is less taxing on staff.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shunichi, would the Study Commons be a ground-floor project? If so, we must check for hazardous materials.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"It is a ground-floor hall. However, it's a conversion, which might be less invasive than a full ventilation overhaul.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, even with that risk, A is more likely to be delivered on time than a ""comfort"" project like C.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Kenji,,I agree. A uses existing space and doesn't require the expensive mechanical plant of D.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, if it's a conversion, it's manageable. It's better than adding more complex systems that need constant upkeep.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"A also fits the profile of the most successful post-occupancy reviews because it's a bookable, shared resource.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Victoria,,Exactly. It solves the room shortage without the massive off-site rental costs of a long-term build.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Logically, A has the fewest points of failure compared to the weather risks of C or the costs of D.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I'm voting for A! It's the most positive and realistic path.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,I can support A. It's a rational use of the budget.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,4,talk,Mizuki,,I vote for A.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,4,talk,Victoria,,I vote for A.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I vote for A.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,4,pass,Kenji,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false}"
69,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,I vote for A.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
